# Docs (`docs/`)

`docs/` is the single documentation root and the Obsidian vault root. The code is the source of truth: when a note disagrees with the code, fix the note; when the code looks wrong, open an issue. Full lifecycle: `docs/SDLC.md` (ADR 0055).

## Layout

| Location | What it holds |
|----------|---------------|
| `docs/HOME.md` | Index of areas only |
| `docs/<AREA>/_INDEX.md` | The area's living design notes (`DESIGN-<TOPIC>.md`), its ADRs and related intents |
| `docs/intent/<YYYY-MM-DD>-<slug>/` | `intent.md` (the problem, in the owner's words), then `spec.md`; frozen once the spec is accepted |
| `docs/adr/NNNN-<slug>.md` | Hard-to-reverse decisions; only the status line changes later (`Superseded by`) |
| `docs/DEVOPS/` | Runbooks |
| `CONTEXT.md` | Glossary: terms only, no code paths |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | The one change log |
| `docs/agents/` | Issue tracker, triage labels, domain-doc usage, learned gotchas |

An ADR starts with `# Title`, then `Status:` (Proposed, Accepted, Rejected, `Superseded by [ADR NNNN](NNNN-slug.md)`, or `Accepted, amended by [ADR NNNN](…)`), `Date:` and, when it replaces or changes another, `Supersedes:` or `Amends:`. The decision text is never edited; only these header lines change.

## Before work

Starting in a domain, or when requirements or history are unclear: read `docs/HOME.md`, the area `_INDEX.md`, the living note and the ADRs it links. Grep `docs/` for the feature, route or model. Use `CONTEXT.md` terms.

## Where a change starts

- A new feature or a change in product behaviour starts as an intent. Bugs, refactors and chores go straight to an issue.
- Settled terms go to `CONTEXT.md`; hard-to-reverse trade-offs become an ADR.

## On ship

1. Add the change to `CHANGELOG.md` under `## [Unreleased]` (the PR hook checks it).
2. Rewrite the area's living design note to describe what the code now does, and keep its `_INDEX.md` line accurate.
3. If the change came from an intent, add `Shipped <date> (#PR)` to its status.

## Writing notes

- One topic per note; extend an existing note before adding one. Living notes describe current behaviour: no phases, TODOs, checklists or history.
- Links between notes are wikilinks from the vault root (`[[ORDERING/DESIGN-WEBSHOP|Web shop]]`, `[[adr/0043-order-rounds-belong-to-dine-in-bills|ADR 0043]]`). Code paths are backticked text.
- Delete outdated notes; do not archive them (git keeps history).
- From `web/` the vault is `../docs/`.
